CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES, FOUNDATION AND BASIC PRINCIPLES
Article 2
The implementation of Protection of Women and Children is based on Pancasila and founded on the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, and is principally based on:
a. respect for human rights, women's human rights and children's rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. protection for confidentiality, security and comfort of victims;
e. the best interests of the child;
f. the right to life, continuity of growth and development, and respect for the child's opinion.

Part Five
Form and Mechanism of Service for Handling Victims of Violence Article 9 (1) Forms of handling services for victims of violence organized by P2TP2A include:
a. medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service, especially Visum et Repertum and Visum et Repertum Psichiatricum, for the purpose of evidence in the judicial process, starting from the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court levels;
c. legal aid services to assist victims of violence in undergoing the judicial process;
d. spiritual services for moral strengthening according to the religion and beliefs adhered to;
e. first psychosocial assistance to victims is carried out to identify the occurrence of violence and trauma experienced by victims; f. assistance to victims of violence carried out by competent persons or institutions that have expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the strengthening and recovery of victims of violence and have cooperated with P2TP2T or other names;
g. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and provision of economic access so that victims can be economically independent; and
h. services to return and or remain in educational institutions for child victims of violence.
(2) The implementation of handling services for women and children victims of violence is carried out: quickly, safely and comfortably, with a sense of empathy, non-discrimination, easily accessible, free of charge and guaranteed confidentiality.
(3) The mechanism and procedures for implementing handling services technically for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) are organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) and further regulated by Regent Regulation.

